/*!
    \title Custom Linear Scale
    \ingroup quickgraphlibdemos
    \brief Demonstrates custom tick formatting for large numbers.
    \example customlinearscale

    \image examples/CustomLinearScale.png

    This example demonstrates how to create custom tick labels for axes when working with large numbers. 
    By using a custom tickDelegate for both X and Y axes, tick values are formatted to display in millions 
    with an "M" suffix (e.g., "20M" instead of "20000000"), making the graph much more readable.

    The example shows:
    - Setting manual tick positions using \c{linspace}
    - Creating custom tick delegates with formatted text
    - Applying the custom formatting to both axes consistently

    \quotefile examples/CustomLinearScale.qml
*/

